  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening project and financial management capacity for HIV/AIDS activities in Central Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the Grant(TF054787)is to test a sub-regional approach to reinforce operational capacity of HIV/AIDS organization managers in order to improve their abilities to conduct task planning, fund raising, financial management, and procuring NGO services, as well contribute to the establishment of informal networks of local organizations in Central Asia which are dealing with HIV/AIDS.  The activities (the Activities) for which the Grant is given are as follows:    (a),,Development and implementation of training program.    (b),,Preparation and distribution of handbooks in local languages on task planning, funding, project implementation, and financial management.    (c),,Development and adoption of strategy on institutionalization of the training program.    (d),,Evaluation of the training program.s impact and its effectiveness. The Grant is designed to increase effectiveness of donor and government-financed projects by covering an area - project management and financial management - that is vital for the long-term sustainability of all current activities but has not yet been tackled. The specific objectives of this Grant would be to test a sub-regional approach to reinforce operational capacity of HIV/AIDS organization managers to conduct efficient project management and address issues of accountability and cost effectiveness.</narrative>
  </description>
